{"engine_version":"0.29.0","file":"araim-gps-galileo.toml","toml":"# Dual-constellation ARAIM availability: GPS + Galileo evaluated with the advanced\n# ARAIM engine, including the constellation-wide fault hypothesis (`araim_dual`).\n#\n# Unlike `integrity-raim.toml` (single-constellation solution-separation RAIM), this\n# runs `araim_dual_raim` at every epoch over a combined GPS + Galileo geometry: the\n# fault-free, single-satellite, AND per-constellation fault hypotheses all feed one\n# MHSS integrity-risk budget (P_HMI). The primary constellation is fault group 0 and\n# each `[[constellations]]` entry the next group.\n#\n# Constellation-fault-robust integrity (staying safe even if an entire constellation\n# fails) is the demanding mode: under the constellation-fault hypothesis the residual\n# constellation must carry the fix alone, so it always costs availability relative to\n# pooling. How much depends on the sky. On the real 2026-06-07 GPS + Galileo catalogue,\n# evaluated at one common epoch, it still reaches 0.990 at a 12 m VAL against 1.000\n# pooled (tests/araim_dual_real_data.rs) — two full constellations can carry it; a\n# depleted one is where a third constellation or SBAS augmentation earns its place.\n# The numerically exact EU ARAIM TN Table A-3 reproduction is an external follow-on\n# (docs/ARAIM_REFERENCE.md).\nkind = \"integrity\"\n\nmask_deg = 5.0\nsigma_uere_m = 0.75   # ISM σ_URA (dual-frequency, m)\np_fa = 1.0e-5         # false-alarm / continuity budget\np_md = 1.0e-3\nal_h_m = 40.0         # horizontal alert limit (APV-I)\nal_v_m = 50.0         # vertical alert limit (APV-I)\naraim_dual = true     # advanced dual-/multi-constellation ARAIM\np_hmi = 1.0e-7        # per-axis integrity-risk budget\n\n[time]\nstep_s = 300.0\nduration_s = 43200.0  # 12 h\n\n[user]\naltitude_km = 0.4\ninclination_deg = 45.0\nraan_deg = 10.0\nu0_deg = 0.0\n\n[constellation]       # GPS-like Walker 24/6/1\naltitude_km = 20200.0\ninclination_deg = 55.0\nplanes = 6\nsats_per_plane = 4\nphasing_f = 1.0\n\n[[constellations]]    # Galileo-like Walker 24/3/1\naltitude_km = 23222.0\ninclination_deg = 56.0\nplanes = 3\nsats_per_plane = 8\nphasing_f = 1.0\n","summary":"integrity | 48 satellites | 145/145 epochs available (100.0%) | HAL 40 m VAL 50 m | sigma 0.8 m | Stanford(V): 0 integrity events, 0 HMI","json":"{\n  \"al_h_m\": 40.0,\n  \"al_v_m\": 50.0,\n  \"samples_total\": 145,\n  \"samples_available\": 145,\n  \"epochs\": [\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 0.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 17,\n      \"hpl_m\": 4.914301432074099,\n      \"vpl_m\": 9.238887604075213,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 300.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 17,\n      \"hpl_m\": 4.717784468058301,\n      \"vpl_m\": 7.465587640919612,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 600.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 15,\n      \"hpl_m\": 5.781570457003854,\n      \"vpl_m\": 6.613776951063681,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 900.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 19,\n      \"hpl_m\": 6.0138687495506975,\n      \"vpl_m\": 6.692617923559769,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 1200.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 15,\n      \"hpl_m\": 5.615201333124597,\n      \"vpl_m\": 11.146835622668455,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 1500.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 16,\n      \"hpl_m\": 6.823197858725306,\n      \"vpl_m\": 10.746015110593135,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 1800.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 14,\n      \"hpl_m\": 7.955393881902287,\n      \"vpl_m\": 11.212861742182188,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 2100.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 14,\n      \"hpl_m\": 6.389754714998125,\n      \"vpl_m\": 13.505926308330103,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 2400.0,\n      \"n_visible\": 19,\n      \"hpl_m\": 4.333055341380723,\n      \"vpl_m\": 7.290999984770419,\n      \"available\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"t_s\": 2700.0,\n      \"n_v